Original commit body from 0a9d0d3476edaf846487b94d18a9b68b4a680506:

ADR-0016 and taint.py both call this vocabulary "hypergumbo's canonical
I/O-boundary risk taxonomy" and six consumers branch on its values, yet it
had none of ADR-0024's four artifacts and io-boundary was absent from
_known_axes(), so no field could even name it. The cost was measured twice:
INV-tutar (env_read carried two readings; 134 of 195 rows misclassified;
22.9% precision on host-secret claims) and WI-johuk (one question derived
four times over five months, ruled zero times, four incompatible censuses,
the only governing text a test docstring).

The axiom is taken VERBATIM from ADR-0049 ruling 1 rather than newly
written, so that ruling stays the value-level ruling and this is the axis
it lives on: a boundary value names what data crosses the process boundary
at this call site, in which direction — not what the program is thereby
arranged to do later.

Four sections over nineteen values. deferred_crossing is a section rather
than a violation: net_listen is precisely what the axiom's second clause
excludes from data_crossing, and ADR-0049 created it deliberately. Two
properties stay per-value because both cut across the partition —
catalog_declarable (the channel split, which makes io_boundary.py's own
"each set is reachable through exactly one channel" comment executable) and
counts_in_headline (subprocess is opaque AND counted, so an axis query
would need exactly one special case).

io_boundary.py no longer writes its five vocabulary constants by hand.
Property tests pin the pre-refactor membership and, for
CATALOG_BOUNDARY_TYPES, the pre-refactor ORDER — _parse_catalog iterates it
and several sites resolve a doubly-declared primitive by
first-declared-wins, so membership equality alone would let a reordering
through.

DISCLOSED NEGATIVE: the drift linter collects nothing on the live tree.
The shared AST walker matches string-literal sets, and the derivation above
removed the last of them, so the linter exits 0 over an empty collection
and would exit 0 identically if it were broken. A synthetic-tree test
proves the scanner fires. The vocabulary's real consumers are dicts and
derived frozensets the walker structurally cannot see
(AUTO_SOURCE_LABEL_MAP, DEFERRED_CROSSING_SHADOWS,
_READ_TARGET_KIND_BOUNDARY); all three get explicit assertions instead,
because a name-filtered scan that silently missed them would look like
coverage. Widening the shared walker serves all four axes and is filed
separately as WI-jinuj.

logging is recorded as the first per-value audit candidate — the one
data_crossing value naming a purpose rather than a medium, overlapping
ipc_send on stdout across 46 rows in 12 catalogues. No row moves.

Also: generate-concept-axes rendered per-axis sections in four copies that
had begun to diverge; extracted to one helper (57 insertions, 0 deletions —
the three existing fields render byte-identically). ADR-0049 was missing
from the README thematic grouping; added alongside 0050.

